(version 1)

# Much of the copper on this board is artwork: the robe, collar and chest plate on the front, and the maker's helmet
# art (moved from his inner layer) on the back. This rule stops DRC from flagging the art for being art; everything
# electrical (pads, tracks, the GND and 3.3 V copper against other nets) is still checked at full rules.
# Rev B is scaled up 1.3x, which gave every part its own space: the rev A rules letting R2, R3, R4 and the XIAO sit
# inside the SAO connector's courtyard, and R4 beside the switch, are gone.

(rule "Fine gaps inside the artwork"
  (condition "A.Type == 'Graphic' && B.Type == 'Graphic'")
  (constraint clearance (min 0.01mm)))
